= El cerco en Acapulco

They have not surrounded a hill. They have surrounded four streets.

Cordons at both ends of the colonia, the navy on the water, the airport road shut, and a loudspeaker vehicle telling people to stay in their houses in the flat voice of a man reading. It is a city cordon, which means it is made of about nine hundred soldiers and police and about four thousand people who live inside it and did not ask for any of this.

You cannot climb out of a city. But a cordon around a colonia is not a ring in the sierra: it is a line drawn on a map by somebody who has never walked these alleys, and it has holes in it that are two feet wide and shaped like a gap between two houses.

- @cer_ac_alcantarilla: **El drenaje.** The storm drains run under the cordon and out into the barranca. *(a way out no soldier will follow you into)*
- @cer_ac_multitud: **La gente.** Make them lift the cordon: get four thousand people into the street at the same time. *(you are asking civilians to face a cordon for you)*
- @foco_batalla.cer_disolverse: **Disolverse.** The column stops existing inside the city and reassembles outside it in a month.
- @foco_batalla.cer_debil: **Salir por lo débil.** Find the thinnest point of the line and go through it.

@cer_ac_alcantarilla
go-to: foco_batalla.cer_fin
