= El cerco en Coyuca

They have finally done the thing that Coyuca has always been waiting for somebody to do: shut both ends of the strip and put boats on the lagoon.

Not many boats. Six, requisitioned, crewed by men who do not know the channels — but six is enough to close the obvious ways, and the obvious ways are the only ones on any chart the navy owns.

The fishermen have been watching this since about four in the morning and one of them is now standing at the edge of the camp, not saying anything, waiting for somebody to ask him.

- @cer_co_barra: **La barra.** Out through the sandbar where the lagoon meets the sea — at night, at the right state of the tide, in boats. *(nobody but the men who fish it can do this; it drowns people who get it wrong)*
- @cer_co_canal: **Los canales.** Not out — *in.* Deep into the mangrove and sit there while they search a lagoon they cannot read. *(safe; you are besieged in a swamp)*
- @foco_batalla.cer_fuerte: **Salir por lo fuerte.** Straight through the strongest point of the highway cordon.
- @foco_batalla.cer_pueblo: **Meterse en el pueblo.** Rifles under floors and become fishermen.

@cer_co_barra
