= El cerco en Atoyac

Every road out of Atoyac is held, which is four roads and one bridge, and there are men on the bridge with a machine gun and a list.

The list is the part that matters. This is not a cordon looking for a column; it is a cordon looking for *names*, and the names are being read off it at every checkpoint by a sergeant with a clipboard, and about a third of them are relatives of people standing in this room.

This is also the town where every single person in the column knows a house. That is the whole difference between being encircled here and being encircled anywhere else in Guerrero.

- @cer_at_casas: **Las casas.** Two here, three there, a hundred and forty houses in a town of ten thousand. Sit it out. *(the deepest use of the water there is; the whole town has to hold)*
- @cer_at_rio: **El río.** Down the riverbed under the bridge itself, at night, in the water. *(directly beneath the machine gun; twenty minutes of absolute silence)*
- @foco_batalla.cer_fuerte: **Salir por lo fuerte.** Through the bridge position, since that is where they least expect it.
- @foco_batalla.cer_disolverse: **Disolverse.** Break up entirely and regather in a month.

@cer_at_casas
