= El cerco en El Quemado

They have closed the road head and put troops on both veredas and on the ridge, and they are not in a hurry, which is new and which is much worse.

A commander who is not in a hurry has understood the actual problem. He is not trying to catch a column in a valley. He is going to sit on the three ways out for as long as it takes and let the arithmetic of food do the work, and while he waits he is going to be in this village, every day, with the list, asking.

And the village has been here before. Everybody in it knows exactly what the next four weeks contain, and they know it in detail, because it has already been done to them once.

- @cer_eq_cuevas: **A la caliza.** Into the caves and wait him out. There is water up there. *(unassailable; you are trading a siege of you for a siege of the village)*
- @cer_eq_entregarse: **Que el pueblo negocie.** Let the village go to him and trade: they give up the *camp* — cold, empty, already stripped — and he lifts the cordon. *(a lie told by two hundred people at once)*
- @foco_batalla.cer_fuerte: **Salir por lo fuerte.** Through the road head and out.
- @foco_batalla.cer_pueblo: **Meterse en el pueblo.** Rifles under the floors, in the houses of people who have already lost everything once.

@cer_eq_cuevas
