= El cerco en Río Chiquito

If they have managed to ring Río Chiquito then they have put men on foot into the middle of the zone and held them there, and that means the war has changed shape while you were busy fighting it.

Nine valleys, every one of them yours in every sense that has ever mattered — and a cordon on all of them, which means the cordon is standing in villages where the guerrilla governs, being watched around the clock by people who have been feeding you for four years and who are, at this moment, doing arithmetic about the rope crossing.

Everybody in those villages knows about the rope crossing. It is a very great deal of people to be relying on.

- @cer_rc_cuerda: **El paso de la cuerda.** The upstream crossing that is not on anything. *(the way out; it exists only as long as nobody says the word)*
- @cer_rc_relevo: **Que el pueblo abra un hueco.** Ask the zone to open one for you — a fire, a stampeded herd, a delegation, an argument that takes an hour. *(the villages take the risk; it is theirs to take)*
- @foco_batalla.cer_fuerte: **Salir por lo fuerte.** Into the strongest sector of the ring.
- @foco_batalla.cer_pueblo: **Meterse en el pueblo.** Into the houses of the zone.

@cer_rc_cuerda
