= El cerco en El Otatal

Nobody has to explain to anybody what this is.

El Otatal, the top of everything, the coffee grove past the end of the survey, ringed — and on the second of December 1974 this is exactly, precisely, in every particular, how it finished for Lucio Cabañas. The column knows. Two people have already said the date out loud without meaning to.

The difference between that morning and this one is not courage and it is not tactics. It is whatever you have spent four years accumulating: the depth of the water, the state of the men, what is in the caches, and whether there is anybody left in these mountains who will lie to a soldier for you.

- @cer_ot_alto: **Por arriba.** Above the grove there is no map and no cordon, because nobody believes a column can cross that. *(three days of rock and cold; it has never been done)*
- @cer_ot_quedarse: **Aquí.** Do not break out. Fight where he fought, with what he did not have. *(the whole war, in one grove, on purpose)*
- @foco_batalla.cer_disolverse: **Disolverse.** The column ceases to exist and regathers in a month, if it does.
- @foco_batalla.cer_debil: **Salir por lo débil.** The thin sector, downhill, toward Río Chiquito.

@cer_ot_alto
